+### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
+*   **Boundary Conditions:** The hardware controller returns 0 for addresses outside the data cube, effectively zero-padding the volume [S1].
+*   **Discretization Artifacts:** The discreteness of precalculated weights can cause visible artifacts. The 6-bit resolution is chosen specifically to make these artifacts invisible to the viewer [S1].
+*   **Memory Limits:** The resampled dataset size is strictly limited to $512^3$ due to gradient buffer constraints [S1].
 
